  "description": "Single source of truth for storage retention (AL-01/AL-04). Declares, per repo-relative directory, the artifact class, TTL, and expiry action enforced by libs/core/storage/storage-janitor.ts. AL-04 extends the AL-01 seed to full coverage of active/shared/runtime/, active/shared/exports/ and active/archive/: every directory is either TTL-governed or declared action=review_required (no automatic deletion; surfaced in the janitor report for a human decision — never a silent forever-retention). Entries with audit=true leave a deletion audit record in active/shared/logs/audit/storage-retention.jsonl; entries with soft_delete_days move expired files to active/archive/.trash/<original-path> for that many further days before the trash sweep purges them. Directories not declared here are never deleted by the janitor; runtime/ subdirectories without an entry are surfaced in the janitor report as uncovered. EV-06 extends coverage beyond active/shared/runtime/ to the append-only event stores (active/shared/observability/, active/shared/coordination/orchestration/events/, presence/bridge/runtime/): these sat outside every janitor scan root, so they were neither TTL-governed nor surfaced as uncovered. scanEventStores enforces their TTLs and listUncoveredEventStoreDirs reports undeclared event streams. WI-10 declares the work-inventory personal/member knowledge subtrees (knowledge/personal/work-inventory, knowledge/personal/members) as never-auto-delete evidence. WI-16 adds an entry-level status_rules vocabulary — a generic, declarative per-file status+age expiry rule nested under a directory entry — and uses it on knowledge/personal/members to expire stale pending_review and discarded work-inventory observation summaries by their own JSON status/date fields (see storage-janitor.ts's sweepStatusRules) without touching confirmed summaries, consents, or unrelated member records. G01/G02/G14 (ops-runtime-retention) declare the top-level ledgers and state files that sit directly in active/shared/runtime/ (dot-*.jsonl, mission_queue.jsonl, reasoning-failover-events.jsonl, …) and the remaining runtime subdirectories; listUncoveredRuntimeEntries now reports undeclared top-level files too (janitor report field uncoveredRuntimeFiles), and the runtime-store-retention check gate (scripts/check/check_runtime_store_retention.ts) fails when source references an active/shared/runtime/<name> store with no entry here. Top-level file entries carry no ttl_days: the janitor's mtime TTL walks directories and an append-only ledger's mtime never ages, so such files are either self-bounded (the note says how) or review_required.",
